[[!comment format=mdwn
 username="joey"
 subject="""comment 4"""
 date="2026-10-06T14:49:50Z"
 content="""
`git-annex export` filters the exported tree to the preferred content of
the remote.

That is not quite what's being asked for here, which is a new feature
to generate a filtered tree. But clearly the code to create such a tree is
all present in git-annex already.

In fact, an export to a special remote does write such a tree to a git ref. 
So a dummy special remote that didn't write any files would be one way to
implement this. (Not a good way.)

I think the question is, what command would it make sense to put this
feature in? And this seems like a good candiate: `git-annex adjust --wanted`
That would adjust the tree to only contain files that are preferred content
of the local repository.

That seems broadly useful. Although similarly to --hide-missing, with
some preferred content expressions (ones using `present`), the adjusted
branch sometimes needs to be updated when content availability changes,
eg after a `git-annex drop`.
"""]]
